WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
Welcome to the video on how to improve apparel and shoe detail pages to reduce returns.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:06.364
Product

00:00:06.364 --> 00:00:10.000
returns are a part of the shopping experience in fashion.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:12.947
As a result, they can have a significant

00:00:12.947 --> 00:00:17.000
impact on customers trust in you as an Amazon selling partner.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:18.714
This video will summarize

00:00:18.714 --> 00:00:23.000
best practices to reduce customer returns of apparel and shoes.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:24.600
Follow this simple step

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:27.000
of reviewing and updating offer attributes.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:30.200
Now it's time to review your existing detail

00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:31.000
page attributes.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:35.125
To improve your existing listing attributes, click on the take action

00:00:35.125 --> 00:00:37.000
button and select edit listing.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:40.667
You will be routed to the listing page five seconds after

00:00:40.667 --> 00:00:45.636
you select edit listing where you can begin updating and improving your existing listing

00:00:45.636 --> 00:00:46.000
attributes.

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:50.588
First, confirm that your listing has sizing options that are accurate and local

00:00:50.588 --> 00:00:52.000
to the US.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:57.895
This is important for both consistency and the customer experience and to help products

00:00:57.895 --> 00:01:00.000
be more discoverable via search.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:03.333
Sizes should be listed in an ascending order from smallest

00:01:03.333 --> 00:01:04.000
to largest.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:09.000
Add additional details for body and height types such as big or tall so customers

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:13.000
have a better understanding of sizing and can choose apparel that fits.

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:14.286
To reduce confusion,

00:01:14.286 --> 00:01:19.000
Amazon has recently updated the size field to a standardized format.

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:20.500
Fill in the corresponding

00:01:20.500 --> 00:01:26.125
required attributes for your product, which will then be automatically combined in a customer-friendly

00:01:26.125 --> 00:01:28.000
format on the display page.

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:32.000
Next, check if your title is accurate and compliant.

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:32.438
Titles

00:01:32.438 --> 00:01:38.125
are critical in both catching a customer's attention and helping identify products through

00:01:38.125 --> 00:01:39.000
Amazon search.

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:43.000
Titles should be concise, informative and accurate.

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:45.273
In general, they include brand

00:01:45.273 --> 00:01:48.000
product type and other identifying information.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:51.556
Titles should not be used to include promotional

00:01:51.556 --> 00:01:52.000
information.

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:56.000
Titles should follow the category-specific Amazon syntax.

00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:57.765
In addition, titles of product

00:01:57.765 --> 00:02:02.000
variants such as size and color should appear on the detail page.

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:04.500
Now let's learn about product

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:05.000
images.

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:10.000
It's crucial to include multiple high-quality images to provide as much clarity to the

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:11.000
customer as possible.

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:16.000
It is recommended that each detail page includes 5 to 7 images.

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:16.400
Please

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:20.000
remember that images should have an all-white background.

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:22.400
Include images that show the product

00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:28.000
from multiple angles, detail shots of key features and wherever possible be on model.

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:28.778
Using multiple

00:02:28.778 --> 00:02:35.000
models and images can help customers better envision the garment on a variety of body types.

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:41.000
Keep in mind that for ASINs that are shared across countries, images will be shared as well.

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:45.000
Please ensure that for these ASINs, images are applicable to all countries.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:46.000
We recommend

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:52.000
including measurement information in both inches and centimeters to address all locations.

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:58.000
Product descriptions and bullet points should be used to provide the customer with additional fit,

00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:02.000
material and product care information not easily conveyed through images.

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:03.000
Whenever possible,

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:06.000
include the following in bullet points.

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:09.000
One, if the product runs large or small.

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:10.333
Two, the model's

00:03:10.333 --> 00:03:13.000
measurements and the corresponding garment size.

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:15.182
Three, specific product measurements.

00:03:15.182 --> 00:03:16.273
For example,

00:03:16.273 --> 00:03:19.000
inseam length or waist size.

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:24.000
Four, styling information such as tight fitting or off the shoulder.

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:24.389
To

00:03:24.389 --> 00:03:30.222
provide a better customer experience, the bullet points in some categories are pulled directly from

00:03:30.222 --> 00:03:31.000
ASIN data.

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:36.652
In shoes, and clothing for example, attributes like material, heel height or sleeve

00:03:36.652 --> 00:03:41.000
type are automatically included to provide customers additional fit information.

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:42.333
Size charts are one

00:03:42.333 --> 00:03:47.000
of the most helpful components of detail pages for customers who have sizing questions.

00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:48.000
Size chart

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:54.000
data should include specific body measurements aligned to their corresponding garment size.

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:58.000
Reach out to seller support to upload your brand specific size chart.

00:03:58.000 --> 00:03:59.833
Size chart widget data is

00:03:59.833 --> 00:04:05.333
automatically shown on product detail pages for all ASINs in the applicable Amazon store that

00:04:05.333 --> 00:04:09.000
share the same brand name, department name and product type.

00:04:09.385 --> 00:04:11.692
Ensure that these values match those

00:04:11.692 --> 00:04:14.000
included in the size selection drop down.

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:17.706
Confirm that all ASINs contain complete and valid attributes

00:04:17.706 --> 00:04:21.000
else the size chart will not be displayed.

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:25.091
A+ content is not only a great place to advertise

00:04:25.091 --> 00:04:30.000
your brand but also a fantastic resource for proactively answering customer questions.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:30.438
For

00:04:30.438 --> 00:04:37.000
example, some brands use a+ content to describe different fit types available with their product.

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:42.895
Another option is to provide styling information such as images of the various ways the product

00:04:42.895 --> 00:04:44.000
can be worn.

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:49.000
Thank you for taking this training on product detail page best practices.

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:49.750
Please remember

00:04:49.750 --> 00:04:55.000
to rate and review this video so that we can continue building useful content.
